      "prov:label": "Data Collection",
      "sc:description": "The game interaction logs were generated by prompting several large language models (LLMs) to play multiple games. We used them to produce step-by-step reasoning and move decisions under a standardized system prompt. A total of 6,443 games were simulated, with the model parameters set to default. All API calls were made via the requests Python package, and the full text responses were collected as raw logs. Initial data are saved as .log files."
    },
    {
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:type": {
        "@id": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5227332"
      },
      "prov:label": "Data Preprocessing",
      "sc:description": "The raw API responses, which included debug information, timestamps, and unstructured text, were transformed into the final structured JSONL dataset through a custom Python preprocessing pipeline. The steps include: (1) parsing each raw log entry to extract the system prompt, user prompt, and the model-generated text; (2) filtering out failed API calls, incomplete responses, or entries that did not contain valid move outputs; (3) structuring the extracted fields into consistent JSON objects with keys 'system_prompt', 'user_prompt', and 'output', matching the exact format of the dataset. No additional text cleaning or normalization beyond the original model output was applied."
    },
    {
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:type": {
        "@id": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q109719325"
      },
      "prov:label": "Annotation",
      "sc:description": "This dataset does not contain any human annotation. All game moves and analyses are generated automatically by the LLM. Win/loss outcomes, where applicable, are derived directly from the rules of Reversi implemented in the simulation environment, without manual labeling."
    }
